Chapter: Fat16Alloc

  cites Foreword chapter Fat16

 The first half of a FAT16 write path: find a free cluster and claim it.

 Two things here are worth a test rather than a reading. The first is that a
 volume carries more than one FAT, and a writer that updates copy 0 and
 forgets copy 1 produces a disk that is wrong in a way nothing on this
 machine would notice -- our own reader consults copy 0. So the test asks
 copy 1 directly, and it asks it before and after, because an allocator that
 never wrote anything and one that wrote both copies both leave copy 0 and
 copy 1 in agreement if you only look once.

 The second is that the scan must not be stuck. block-sector-count returned 0
 on every disk for as long as it existed and looked exactly like a working
 counter, because nothing ever demanded a specific number from it twice. So
 this test allocates, then scans again: the second free cluster must not be
 the first one. An allocator whose write silently did nothing returns the
 same cluster forever, and that is the failure this line is here to catch.

 We say:

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Device.Block] Nothing
  opening = act
    vol <- fat16-init 2048
    print-line-uni ("usable " & show (fat16-vol-is-usable vol))
    print-line-uni ("fats " & show (vol.vol-num-fats))
    print-line-uni ("clusters " & show (vol.vol-cluster-count))

    free1 <- fat16-find-free-cluster vol
    print-line-uni ("free-found " & show (free1 > 0))

    before0 <- fat16-read-fat-entry vol 0 free1
    before1 <- fat16-read-fat-entry vol 1 free1
    print-line-uni ("before-copy0 " & show before0)
    print-line-uni ("before-copy1 " & show before1)

    got <- fat16-alloc-cluster vol
    print-line-uni ("claimed-what-it-found " & show (got == free1))

    after0 <- fat16-read-fat-entry vol 0 got
    after1 <- fat16-read-fat-entry vol 1 got
    print-line-uni ("after-copy0 " & show after0)
    print-line-uni ("after-copy1 " & show after1)
    print-line-uni ("copies-agree " & show (after0 == after1))
    print-line-uni ("is-end " & show (fat16-is-end after0))

    free2 <- fat16-find-free-cluster vol
    print-line-uni ("second-differs " & show (free2 /= free1))
  end
